==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{der|is|non|hvenær}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈkʰvɛːnair/|/ˈxʷɛː/|q2=dialectal, now rare}}

===Adverb===
{{head|is|adverb}}

# [[when]]
#: {{ux|is|'''Hvenær''' er von á þér?|'''When''' may we expect you?}}
#: {{ux|is|'''Hvenær''' áttu afmæli?|'''When''' is your birthday?}}

====Usage notes====
This word is only used as an interrogative pronoun. In statements, the word ''{{l|is|þegar}}'' is used.

==Old Norse==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|non|hvenar}} (in the [[w:en:Droplaugarsona saga|Droplaugarsona saga]])
* {{l|non|hvener}}

===Etymology===
Likely an exact cognate to {{cog|nl|wanneer|t=when}}. De Vries, however, prefers a derivation from {{af|non|[[hve|hvé]]|nær|t1=how|t2=near}}, with sense development "how near" > "how early" > "when". The first component is regardless related to {{cog|gem-pro|*hwan|t=when}}.<ref>{{R:non:AnEW|page=271|head=hvénær, hvénar, hvéner}}</ref>

